# LeakSanitizer suppressions for known leaks.
#
# CTest passes this file to the tests in builds with
# WITH_COMPILER_ASAN=ON (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...).  Remove an
# entry when its bug is fixed.  Suppressions match function names, so
# they need a symbolizer (llvm-symbolizer, or addr2line through
# ASAN_SYMBOLIZER_PATH, which CTest sets up when there is no
# llvm-symbolizer).

# libXt: the 104-byte record that XtOwnSelection() and
# XtDisownSelection() allocate for a selection is not freed when its
# widget is destroyed.  Seen from every Motif selection owner: the text
# widgets (PRIMARY through XmeNamedSource, MOTIF_DESTINATION through
# XmeSecondarySink and df_SetDestination, the destroy callback
# DisownCallback) and the clipboard (AssertClipboardSelection).  Not
# known to be Motif's fault.
leak:XtOwnSelection
leak:XtDisownSelection

# fontconfig: the configuration that FcInit loads, the first time Xft
# opens a font, is kept until FcFini, which no X client calls.
leak:libfontconfig.so

# libXm: when an XmNnoFontCallback gives the rendition it is called with
# (the first of the widget's render table) a font with
# XmRenditionUpdate, the rendition gets new data, and XmString.c
# (OptLineMetrics and SpecifiedSegmentExtents, which "split the ref
# counts") sets the reference count of the old data to the number of its
# other holders, often 0, without freeing it: one rendition per label.
# The RenderTable suite's no_font_callback_when_drawn makes that happen
# on purpose; the library before the render table cache leaks the same.
leak:no_font_callback_when_drawn_fn
